<%--
Api_Scope_Preview - the effective-access panel for one API scope rule set.

Answers "what can a key carrying these rules actually call", by resolving the rule text
against the real baked API route table (Api_Catalog::resolve_for_scopes) rather than by
asking the operator to read globs. It is the same panel in both places it is needed: live
under the mint form as rules are typed, and read-only when viewing an existing key.

Arguments:
- $scopes (string|null): the rule text to resolve. Null or blank means UNRESTRICTED, which
  this panel says in words rather than by listing the whole surface as though it had been
  granted rule by rule.
- $blank_is_unrestricted (bool, default true): what a blank $scopes MEANS here. False while
  a mint form is in Scoped mode with nothing chosen yet: an operator who has said "scoped"
  and written no rule has selected NOTHING, and telling them they have unrestricted access
  would be the opposite of the truth.

Refreshing: the owner sets `preview.args.scopes` and calls `reload()`. The fetch lives in
on_load(), so every refresh is one round trip and the panel cannot fetch from a handler.

Usage:
    <Api_Scope_Preview $sid="preview" $scopes=null />
--%>
<Define:Api_Scope_Preview tag="div">
    <div class="Api_Scope_Preview__title">Effective access</div>

    <% if (this.data.error) { %>
        <div class="Api_Scope_Preview__error">
            <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle-fill"></i>
            <span><%= this.data.error %></span>
        </div>
    <% } else if (this.data.unrestricted) { %>
        <div class="Api_Scope_Preview__note">
            Unrestricted - this key reaches every endpoint its holder's permissions allow.
        </div>
    <% } else if (!this.data.groups.length) { %>
        <div class="Api_Scope_Preview__note">
            No endpoints. A key with these rules can call nothing.
        </div>
    <% } else { %>
        <div class="Api_Scope_Preview__groups">
            <% for (const group of this.data.groups) { %>
                <div class="Api_Scope_Preview__group">
                    <div class="Api_Scope_Preview__group_name"><%= group.name %></div>
                    <% for (const endpoint of group.endpoints) { %>
                        <div class="Api_Scope_Preview__endpoint">
                            <span class="Api_Scope_Preview__method Api_Scope_Preview__method--<%= endpoint.method.toLowerCase() %>"><%= endpoint.method %></span>
                            <span class="Api_Scope_Preview__path"><%= endpoint.pattern %></span>
                        </div>
                    <% } %>
                </div>
            <% } %>
        </div>
    <% } %>
</Define:Api_Scope_Preview>
